AU  - Hawkins, Joseph E.; Johnsson, Lars-Göran; Stebbins, William C.; Moody, David B.; Coombs, Sheryl
TI  - Hearing Loss and Cochlear Pathology in Monkeys After Noise Exposure
PY  - 1976
AB  - Old World monkeys were exposed to octave-band noise from 0.5 to 8 kHz at 120 dB SPL, 8 hours daily for 20 days. Restricted permanent threshold shifts and localized loss of outer hair cells were produced, which were reasonably well correlated with the exposure frequencies. There was also a loss of both inner and outer hair cells at the extreme basal end of Corti's organ, regardless of the exposure frequency. Implications for human inner ear pathology are discussed.
